"""tinyland_converge_agent — the pull-shaped production-convergence
carrier, authored once and instantiated per tenant.

Realizes site.scaffold docs/patterns/converge-agent.md and
docs/patterns/stateful-workload-convergence.md §2 (one published module,
N instantiations). Publication target: tinyland-inc/bazel-registry per the
TIN-2030 extraction mechanism — steps documented in README.md, executed only
as a separately reviewed registry PR.

This module ships shell, YAML-template, and tofu sources plus a
stdlib-Python contract test. It carries exactly one bazel_dep,
rules_shell - see BUILD.bazel's own header: native sh_test/sh_binary/
sh_library autoload only applies within a Bazel invocation's MAIN
repository, so this package's own `load("@rules_shell//shell:sh_test.bzl",
"sh_test")` needs this module's OWN repo mapping to resolve, once anything
outside this repository depends on it as an external module (which its
own README section "Consuming through the registry" documents as the
supported path). Discovered empirically consuming this module from MMS
#71/TIN-489, 2026-08-08.
"""

module(
    name = "tinyland_converge_agent",
    version = "0.1.0",
    compatibility_level = 1,
)

bazel_dep(name = "rules_shell", version = "0.8.0")
